Attribution
===========

This package contains no data and no mappings. It is a vocabulary: a handful of
classes and two canonical identifier predicates that other packages align into.

Nothing here is derived from a third-party vocabulary. The classes are
deliberately NAMED after well-known terms — `Organization` and `Person` mean
what FOAF, schema.org and W3C ORG mean by those words — but no third-party
definition is copied, imported, or redistributed, and installing this package
pulls in no external file. The resemblance is adoption as influence, not as
dependency: a consumer who wants `foaf:Organization owl:equivalentClass
party:Organization` asserts that edge in their own workspace, where it costs
only them.

"LEI" refers to the ISO 17442 Legal Entity Identifier and to the Global LEI
System operated by GLEIF. This package names the identifier; it redistributes no
LEI data and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or produced in cooperation
with GLEIF or ISO.

